<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan May forex reserves rise to $1.743 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan May forex reserves rise to $1.743 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves rose to $1.743 billion in May from $1.567 billion in April, compared to $2.141 billion in May 1996, the State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The bank gave no reason for the rise but one banker attributed it to remittances from Pakistanis working abroad.</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
